        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "### B. Challenges Specific to Catheters",
            "block_bbox": [
                619,
                692,
                921,
                715
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 11,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    619.0,
                    692.0
                ],
                [
                    921.0,
                    692.0
                ],
                [
                    921.0,
                    715.0
                ],
                [
                    619.0,
                    715.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Catheters present challenges absent in rigid-body robots. Model uncertainty: the mechanics follow a variant of the Cosserat rod equations [3], [4], with distributed elasticity, sheath friction, tendon backlash, and hysteresis that vary widely across specimens, making full-model inversion impractical. Cardiac motion: the heart moves  $ \\sim $10–15 mm per cycle at  $ \\sim $1 Hz; after gross target tracking, the local residual wall-normal motion still produces quasi-periodic contact-force disturbances with known frequency but unknown phase and amplitude. Limited sensing: most clinical catheters carry no force sensor; tip position is available via electromagnetic (EM) tracking, fluoroscopy, or intracardiac echocardiography at moderate latency (10–50 ms). Safety criticality: a perforation force threshold of  $ \\sim $0.3–0.5 N is clinically relevant [12], making hard force-constraint enforcement—not soft penalization—essential.",
            "block_bbox": [
                617,
                721,
                1131,
                1103
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 12,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    617.0,
                    721.0
                ],
                [
                    1131.0,
                    721.0
                ],
                [
