                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Catheter and continuum-robot control has progressed from PID and Jacobian-based kinematic regulation [5], [6] to modelless feedback [6] and predictive interaction-dynamics optimization. Cosserat-based predictive control can model rich catheter dynamics but requires online nonlinear-program solution, limiting update rates to  $ \\sim $10–20Hz. Constant-curvature kinematics [2] underlie most reduced-order interaction models. Learning-based approaches improve robustness to model uncertainty but usually do not provide formal stability or hard interaction-constraint guarantees.",
            "block_bbox": [
                616,
                1164,
                1130,
                1401
            ],
            "block_id": 14,
            "block_order": 12,
            "group_id": 14,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    616.0,
                    1164.0
                ],
                [
                    1130.0,
                    1164.0
                ],
                [
                    1130.0,
